    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: kimi-code 0.27.0

Kimi Code, Moonshot AI's command-line coding agent (MIT). Packaged from the
self-contained npm bundle; the interactive shell backend (node-pty 1.1.0) is
compiled from source offline with node-addon-api 7.1.1 as a vendored native
addon. Runtime code search uses the system ripgrep and fd.

Built for Leap 16.0/aarch64 with 0 rpmlint badness, source_validator clean,
%check (kimi --version) passes. ExclusiveArch x86_64 aarch64 (native addon).</comment>
    <requestid>1366481</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>4336d4d74f6c7c52edc2bc9dea007e21</srcmd5>
    <version>0.31.1</version>
    <time>1785872011</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to kimi-code 0.31.1.

Eight upstream releases since 0.27.0 (0.28.0 through 0.31.1). Headline
change is the removal of the 'kimi server' command tree in favour of a
foreground-only 'kimi web'; the rest is custom agents, model catalog
imports and a large batch of session/turn fixes -- see the changelog.

The vendored node-pty (1.1.0) and node-addon-api (7.1.1) are unchanged:
upstream still declares node-pty ^1.1.0 as an optional dependency and
1.1.0 is still the newest release. Verified with a local osc build for
openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: green, %check runs the installed binary and
reports 0.31.1, rpmlint 0 errors 0 warnings 0 badness, source_validator
clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1369256</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>94acad792d5d59a2750e3e1c3ca2367e</srcmd5>
    <version>0.34.0</version>
    <time>1786304648</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to version 0.34.0 (0.32.0, 0.33.0, 0.34.0): the CLI surfaces now run on the agent-core-v2 engine by default (KIMI_CODE_LEGACY_FLAG=1 falls back), new hook events, a [token_counting] config section, MCP OAuth re-authorization and structuredContent fixes, and 'kimi -p' now waits for background tasks. node-pty stays at 1.1.0 (upstream still asks for ^1.1.0; 1.2.0 is beta-only) and node-addon-api at 7.1.1. Built and verified on aarch64: %check runs 'kimi --version' successfully, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370306</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c09ff66686d15cd22cb00b07878226cd</srcmd5>
    <version>0.36.1</version>
    <time>1786826503</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update kimi-code to 0.36.1 (npm @moonshot-ai/kimi-code, published 2026-08-14).

Covers upstream releases 0.35.0, 0.36.0 and 0.36.1:
- new experimental fullscreen TUI mode (KIMI_CODE_TUI_FULL_SCREEN=1) and a
  configurable secondary-model pool for spawned subagents
- live subagent progress in /tasks, LaTeX formula rendering, MCP OAuth
  auto-detection and connection refresh after credential changes
- workspace-trust hardening: project MCP launch targets are shown, trust
  defaults to declined, and fd/stty/git/gh are resolved to absolute paths so
  an untrusted workspace cannot plant bare-name executables
- numerous session/provider fixes (tool-call id renumbering, interrupted
  thinking turns, post-compaction token counts, startup freezes) and a
  reworked web UI

Packaging is unchanged apart from Version:. The vendored node-pty (1.1.0) and
node-addon-api (7.1.1) pins were re-checked against the ranges upstream
declares (node-pty ^1.1.0, node-addon-api ^7.1.0) and both remain the newest
matching stable releases. License is still MIT (LICENSE file byte-identical).

Built locally against openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: green, rpmlint 0 errors,
0 warnings, 0 badness (11 filtered), and %check ran `kimi --version` which
printed 0.36.1.</comment>
    <requestid>1371320</requestid>
  </revision>
